                           FIBRE GEOMETRY OF A CUT-DEPENDENT
                             CROSSING-COMPONENT RETRACTION


                                                       ANONYMOUS


         Abstract. Fix a cut in a chord matching and, simultaneously for every component of its crossing graph,
         replace the component by consecutive pairs on the same endpoint support. This is a one-step retraction
         onto noncrossing matchings. For a target matching T , its nesting forest turns the inverse problem into
         independent choices on the ordered lists of immediate siblings. We prove an all-size bijection: partition
         each sibling list noncrossingly and decorate every part by a crossing-connected matching. It gives the
         pointwise fibre product                             Y
