Proof. Equation (2) makes every image noncrossing. A noncrossing matching has singleton crossing
components and is unchanged, proving the retraction statements and the Catalan count. If Φ(y) = x
then Φ(x) = Φ2 (y) = x, so a nonfixed x has no predecessor. Finally every positive iterate has the
same Catn fixed points, which gives the stated fixed-n Artin–Mazur zeta function. These are formal
consequences of a one-step retraction and receive no contribution credit.                       □

